---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<!--
  Table Tennis OS — private demo page for clubs.
  Deliberately kept out of sitemap.xml, the nav, and search engines (noindex):
  it's a link Joel shares directly with other clubs.
-->
<Base
  title="Table Tennis OS | Acceso AI"
  description="The operating software behind Devonport Table Tennis: fixtures, results, live ladders, member logins and a full admin panel, in one website. See the live demo and get it for your club."
  path="/table-tennis-os/"
  noindex={true}
>
  <!-- ═══ PAGE HERO ═════════════════════ -->
  <div class="hero-shell">
    <canvas class="net-canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <header class="page-hero wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow hero-fade"><span class="idx">01</span> <span data-scramble="">Table Tennis OS</span></p>
      <h1 data-split="hero">One website that <em>runs the whole club.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede hero-fade">
        Fixtures, results, live ladders, player averages, memberships, member
        logins and a committee admin panel, all in one place. This is the
        software that runs Devonport Table Tennis every week, and your club
        can have it too.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-ctas hero-fade">
        <a href="https://devtt.com.au/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-ink">
          See it live at devtt.com.au
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 4.5 21 12m0 0-7.5 7.5M21 12H3"></path></svg>
        </a>
        <a href="mailto:Joel@bakerswalkingco.au" class="btn btn-line">Talk to us about your club</a>
      </div>
    </header>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══ DEVICES ═══════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section wrap" style="padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);">
    <div class="case-devices rv">
      <div class="device-laptop">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <img src="/table-tennis-os/tt-home.jpg" alt="Table Tennis OS on a laptop: the club homepage showing this week's fixtures for both competition nights" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <div class="device-base"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="device-phone">
        <img src="/table-tennis-os/tt-home-mobile.jpg" alt="The same site on a phone, where most members use it" loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="img-caption case-devices-caption">Live right now at devtt.com.au · every screenshot on this page is the real site, captured this week</p>

    <div class="case-body">
      <p class="rv">
        Most clubs run a season the same way: the draw in a spreadsheet,
        results typed up and passed around, ladders recalculated by hand, and
        the whole thing living in the heads of one or two dedicated
        volunteers. It works, until that person is away.
      </p>
      <p class="rv">
        Table Tennis OS replaces all of it with one website. The season draw
        is published once, results are entered once, and everything else, the
        ladders, the percentages, the player averages, updates on its own.
        Members check their phone on the way to the clubrooms. The committee
        runs the competition from a single admin panel.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ WHAT MEMBERS SEE ══════════════ -->
  <section class="section wrap" id="tour">
    <p class="eyebrow rv"><span class="idx">02</span> <span data-scramble="">The Tour</span></p>
    <h2 class="display" data-split="" style="margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);">
      What your members <em>see.</em>
    </h2>

    <div class="shot-grid">
      <figure class="shot rv">
        <img src="/table-tennis-os/tt-fixtures.jpg" alt="Fixtures and results page with live ladders for every grade, searchable by player or team" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption>
          <strong>Fixtures, results &amp; live ladders.</strong> The full season
          draw for every night and grade, with ladders and player percentages
          that update the moment results go in. Searchable by player or team.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot rv">
        <img src="/table-tennis-os/tt-new-here.jpg" alt="New Here page welcoming first-time players with a free first visit and practice session times" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption>
          <strong>A front door for new players.</strong> A dedicated landing
          page that turns curious locals into members: first hit free, session
          times, and exactly what to expect on their first night.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot rv">
        <img src="/table-tennis-os/tt-membership.jpg" alt="Online membership form that takes about two minutes" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption>
          <strong>Memberships, online.</strong> New members and renewals
          through a two-minute form. The treasurer gets the details, the
          member gets an invoice and a login. No paper forms.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot rv">
        <img src="/table-tennis-os/tt-learn.jpg" alt="Learn page with coach profiles and technique videos" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption>
          <strong>Coaching &amp; learning.</strong> Coach profiles, session
          times and hand-picked technique videos, so improving isn't limited
          to one night a week.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot rv">
        <img src="/table-tennis-os/tt-contact.jpg" alt="Contact page with the clubrooms address and a simple message form" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption>
          <strong>Contact &amp; club info.</strong> One obvious place for
          session times, the clubrooms address and a message form that goes
          straight to the committee.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot rv">
        <img src="/table-tennis-os/tt-login.jpg" alt="Member login page for the members-only area" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption>
          <strong>Member logins.</strong> Behind the login, members get their
          own dashboard: their upcoming matches, their results and averages,
          club events they can sign up to, and their availability for the
          season. The committee gets a full admin panel: results upload,
          announcements, events, memberships and more.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ BEFORE / AFTER ════════════════ -->
  <section class="section wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow rv"><span class="idx">03</span> <span data-scramble="">The Change</span></p>
    <h2 class="display" data-split="" style="margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);">
      From spreadsheets to <em>one system.</em>
    </h2>

    <div class="outcome rv">
      <div class="outcome-grid">
        <div class="outcome-side before">
          <p class="outcome-label">Before</p>
          <ul class="outcome-list">
            <li>Season draw kept in spreadsheets and printouts</li>
            <li>Results typed up and passed around by hand</li>
            <li>Ladders and averages recalculated manually each week</li>
            <li>Paper membership forms chased up every season</li>
            <li>Everything dependent on one or two volunteers</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="outcome-side after">
          <p class="outcome-label">After</p>
          <ul class="outcome-list">
            <li>Fixtures, results and ladders live on one website</li>
            <li>Results entered once, everything updates instantly</li>
            <li>Members join and renew online, and log in to their own dashboard</li>
            <li>The committee runs the whole competition from one admin panel</li>
            <li>The club's history stays with the club, not in someone's head</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-result">
        <span class="k">The Result</span>
        <span class="v">A volunteer committee runs a full pennant season without the paperwork.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ul class="about-facts rv" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <li>Fixtures &amp; results</li>
      <li>Live ladders</li>
      <li>Player averages</li>
      <li>Online memberships</li>
      <li>Member dashboards</li>
      <li>Events &amp; announcements</li>
      <li>Committee admin panel</li>
      <li>Built with AI</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ FOR YOUR CLUB ═════════════════ -->
  <section class="section wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow rv"><span class="idx">04</span> <span data-scramble="">Your Club</span></p>
    <h2 class="display" data-split="" style="margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);">
      Set up for <em>your club.</em>
    </h2>
    <div class="case-body">
      <p class="rv">
        Table Tennis OS isn't a template you squeeze your competition into.
        It was built around how a local pennant season actually works, nights,
        grades, byes, percentages, finals, and it gets set up around yours:
        your name, your colours, your grades, your roster, on your own web
        address.
      </p>
      <p class="rv">
        Because it's built and run with AI, it costs what a volunteer
        committee can actually say yes to, not what league-management software
        usually costs. Have a click around the live site first, then get in
        touch and we'll talk through what it would look like for your club.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ FINALE ════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="finale section" id="contact">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow rv"><span data-scramble="">Get Started</span></p>
      <h2 data-split="">Want this for <em>your club?</em></h2>
      <p class="lede rv">Explore the live site at devtt.com.au, then tell us about your club. We'll show you exactly what your version would look like.</p>
      <div class="finale-ctas rv">
        <a href="https://devtt.com.au/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-paper">
          See the live demo
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 4.5 21 12m0 0-7.5 7.5M21 12H3"></path></svg>
        </a>
        <a href="mailto:Joel@bakerswalkingco.au" class="btn btn-ghost-dark">Contact Acceso AI</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .shot-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .shot-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .shot {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .shot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 10px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.12);
    box-shadow: 0 18px 40px -22px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.35);
  }
  .shot figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--muted, #55607a);
  }
  .shot figcaption strong {
    color: var(--ink, #101828);
  }
</style>
